{"question_text": {"৪৮তম বিশেষ বিসিএস [স্বাস্থ্য] – মেডিকেল অংশ": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Who is considered the father of surgery? ", "option1": "Abu Al-Zahrawi", "option2": "Sushruta", "option3": "Joseph Lister", "option4": "Ambroise Parè", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_980450271431750466320047.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Which is an advantage of minimal access surgery? ", "option1": "Improved mobility", "option2": "3D vision ", "option3": "Haemostasis ", "option4": "Excellent tactile feedback ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_748018780431750444677964.png\" />"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which is not a component of preoperative airway assessment? ", "option1": "Mallampati score ", "option2": "Mouth opening ", "option3": "Neck flexion", "option4": "Thyromental distance ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_380142645431750466387726.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) What is the guideline for preoperative fasting in adults? ", "option1": "4 hours for clear fluids ", "option2": "4 hour for non-clear fluids ", "option3": "6 hours for solid foods ", "option4": "Minimum 8 hours for solid food ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_514819981431750465823316.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Which of the following drugs should be stopped 24 hours prior to an elective surgery in patients with IHD? ", "option1": "Aspirin ", "option2": "Beta-blocker ", "option3": "Statin ", "option4": "Angiotensin receptor blocker ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_59228493431750515778802.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Which anticoagulant should be used in the perioperative period in patients with mechanical heart valves? ", "option1": "Unfractionated heparin ", "option2": "Low molecular weight heparin ", "option3": "Warfarin ", "option4": "Rivaroxaban ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_500753005431750466739643.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Which is the first step in managing a polytrauma patient? ", "option1": "Airway and cervical spine protection ", "option2": "Control of massive external hemorrhage ", "option3": "Breathing and ventilation ", "option4": "Maintaining circulation ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_820465342431750467134421.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Which is the ideal fluid for resuscitation of severely hypovolemic trauma patients? ", "option1": "Normal saline ", "option2": "Whole blood ", "option3": "Hartmann's solution ", "option4": "Fresh frozen plasma ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_812395637431750467635092.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Which organ is most commonly injured in blunt abdominal trauma? ", "option1": "Spleen ", "option2": "Liver ", "option3": "Kidney ", "option4": "Transverse colon ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_921902394431750524605358.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which is the most common cause of compartment syndrome? ", "option1": "Soft tissue contusion ", "option2": "Tight plaster ", "option3": "Closed fractures ", "option4": "Circumferential burn ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_492950025431750524673119.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Which of the followings is not associated with impaired wound healing? ", "option1": "Vitamin-C deficiency", "option2": "Diabetes mellitus ", "option3": "Radiotherapy ", "option4": "Conn's syndrome", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_685600286441750524766387.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_712560873431750524759137.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Example of clean contaminated wound is- ", "option1": "Herniotomy ", "option2": "Cholecystectomy ", "option3": "Perforated peptic ulcer ", "option4": "Burst appendix ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_12421561501750524826812.png\" />"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Hydrocolloid transparent dressing serves as- ", "option1": "Mechanical debridement ", "option2": "Enzymatic debridement ", "option3": "Autolytic debridement ", "option4": "Biological debridement ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_237384834431750524879877.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Which is the first line treatment option for hypertrophic scar? ", "option1": "Intralesional corticosteroid ", "option2": "Cryosurgery", "option3": "Laser therapy ", "option4": "Silicone gel ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_791838971441750524961140.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_429138495431750524954456.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Which is the most common sourse of surgical site infection? ", "option1": "Hospital staff ", "option2": "OT environment ", "option3": "Endogenous organisms ", "option4": "Unsterile instruments ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_545527302431750524985318.png\" />"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Which is the minimum time required to form an abscess after a surgery? ", "option1": "2 days ", "option2": "3 days ", "option3": "5 days ", "option4": "7 days ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_819657061431750525080573.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Which is an immediatele life threatening condition following chest trauma? ", "option1": "Flail chest ", "option2": "Closed aortic injuries ", "option3": "Myocardial contusion ", "option4": "Rupture of the diaphragm ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_456609306431750520681056.png\" />"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Necrotising fasciitis is most commonly associated with-", "option1": "Staphylococcus aureus ", "option2": "Clostridium perfringenes ", "option3": "Streptococcus pyogenes ", "option4": "Anaeroboic organisms ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_275201092431750525189171.png\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Which of these agents is not routinely used for skin preparation before surgery? ", "option1": "Povidone iodine ", "option2": "Chlorhexidine ", "option3": "70% ethanol ", "option4": "Cetrimide ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_547768146431750525258334.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Exotoxin responsible for destruction of the muscle cells in gas gangrene- ", "option1": "Kappa toxin", "option2": "Alpha-toxin", "option3": "Phi-toxin ", "option4": "Beta-toxin ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_359972769431750525333351.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Which is not included in the diagnostic criteria of SIRS? ", "option1": "Temperature <36° C ", "option2": "White cell < 4000/mm³", "option3": "Heart rate <60/min. ", "option4": "Respiratory rate >20/min. ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_671254099431750525356664.png\" />"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) All are causes of cardiogenic shock except- ", "option1": "Blunt myocardial injury ", "option2": "Cardiomyopathy", "option3": "Cardiac arrhythmia ", "option4": "Cardiac tamponade ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_472249104431750525413387.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Which is not consistent with compensated shock? ", "option1": "Lactic acidosis ", "option2": "Oliguria ", "option3": "Normal blood pressure ", "option4": "Tachypnea ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_473611747431750525436076.png\" />"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Reactionary hemorrhage is caused by- ", "option1": "Sloughing of the vessel wall", "option2": "Slippage of ligature ", "option3": "Pressure from drain ", "option4": "Infection ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_131204232431750525500413.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Which is the best monitor of adequacy of shock therapy? ", "option1": "Cardiac output ", "option2": "Central venous pressure ", "option3": "Urine output ", "option4": "Invasive blood pressure ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_236930720431750525570727.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Which is not a complication of massive blood transfusion? ", "option1": "Hypokalaemia ", "option2": "Hypothermia ", "option3": "Hyperkalaemia ", "option4": "Hypercalcemia ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_358256484431750525607775.png\" />"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Which is an example of biological hemostatic agent? ", "option1": "Bone wax ", "option2": "Tranexamic acid ", "option3": "Gelatin ", "option4": "Absorbable collagen ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_976319329431750525632139.png\" />"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Which is a content of Littre's hernia? ", "option1": "Vermiform appendix ", "option2": "Part of Bowel wall", "option3": "Meckel's diverticulum ", "option4": "Urinary bladder ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_370966476431750525691382.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Which does not form the boundary of the Hesselbach's triangle? ", "option1": "Inferior epigastric vessels ", "option2": "Arcuate line ", "option3": "Lateral border of rectus muscle ", "option4": "Inguinal ligament ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_120748291431750525712565.png\" />"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Which is an example of primary ventral hernia? ", "option1": "Inguinal hernia ", "option2": "Incisional hernia ", "option3": "Parastomal hernia ", "option4": "Epigastric hernia", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_875281058431750525733147.png\" />"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) Which is not consistent with indirect inguinal hernia? ", "option1": "Is usually complete ", "option2": "Is easily reducible ", "option3": "Deep ring occlusion test is negative ", "option4": "Is always acquired ", "answer": "0", "exp": "<p>প্রশ্নে ভুল থাকায় প্রশ্নটি বাতিল করা হলো।&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_379565161431750525802680.jpg\" /></p>"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Which is the most common immediate cause of death from fire? ", "option1": "Hypovolemic shock ", "option2": "Neurogenic shock ", "option3": "Carbon monoxide poisoning ", "option4": "Airway obstruction", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_611153455431750525871322.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) Full thickess burn is characterized by- ", "option1": "Reduced sensation ", "option2": "Blistering ", "option3": "Delayed capillary filling ", "option4": "Hard leathery feel", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_638421399441750525975808.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_503814598431750525969635.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) What is the crystalloid requirement in the first 24 hours  in a 60kg male with 20% burn? ", "option1": "4800 ml ", "option2": "7200 ml ", "option3": "3600 ml ", "option4": "2400 ml ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_621438623431750526044512.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) Which is not a premalignant lesion of the skin? ", "option1": "Giant congenital pigemented naevus ", "option2": "Blue naevus ", "option3": "Extramammary Paget's disease ", "option4": "Dysplastic naevus ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_321473152431750526108989.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) Which is the most common form of skin cancer? ", "option1": "Squamous cell carcinoma ", "option2": "Basal cell carcinoma ", "option3": "Malignant melanoma ", "option4": "Sebaceous carcinoma ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_239241868431750526181609.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) Which is the most important prognostic indicator in maliganat melanoma? ", "option1": "Tumour size ", "option2": "Change in shape ", "option3": "Breslow thickness ", "option4": "Lympahatic involvement ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_773391764441750526299807.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_652586849431750526293736.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) Transillumination test is negative in- ", "option1": "Epididymal cyst ", "option2": "Ranula ", "option3": "Meningocele ", "option4": "Sebaceous cyst", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_370597223431750526351994.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "39", "question": "৩৯) Treatment of hyperkalaemia includes all, but- ", "option1": "Infusion of 10% calcium gluconate ", "option2": "Diuresis by injectable spironolactone ", "option3": "Salvutamol nebulization ", "option4": "Insulin administration ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_28368829441750526461599.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_988574904431750526455930.jpg\" />"}, {"id": "40", "question": "৪০) Hypokalaemia can occur as a result of- ", "option1": "Renal failure ", "option2": "Adrenal insufficiency ", "option3": "Metabolic acidosis ", "option4": "Ureterosigmoidostomy ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_147682729441750526552784.jpg\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceu_459567368431750526546592.jpg\" />"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 11521, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "1200000", "is_omr": true, "omr_time": "1440000", "examname": "Jun 22, 2025", "type": "BCS-Health-Medic", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}